Put all four in a new group called Clean Energy, so they are easy to find when adding them to libraries.
Shared values, identical on every site:
• Document Status: Active, Archive
• Technology: Solar, Wind, Storage, Not technology specific
Local values, different on every site:
• Library: that site's library names, spelled exactly as the libraries are named
• Document Category: that site's top level folder names, excluding Archive folders
Set Allow fill in choices to No on all four. Fill in choices are how spelling drifts and filter values split in two.
Step 6. Libraries, columns and defaults
For every library that will hold documents:
1. Library settings, Add from existing site columns. Add all four from the Clean Energy group.
2. Library settings, Column default value settings. This page shows the library root at the top and the folder tree beneath it.
3. On the library root, set Library to that library's name and Document Status to Active.
4. On each top level folder, set Document Category to the folder's name.
5. On any technology folder, set Technology.
6. On any Archive folder, set Document Status to Archive. Leave its Category empty.
Watch out for the default Documents library. Every site gets one, and the name is identical across all four sites. Either keep it empty or give it a site specific name, or you will get one meaningless Documents entry in the hub Library filter covering every site.
Defaults only apply to new files. Anything already in the library needs tagging by hand: open the folder, switch to Edit in grid view, fill the first row, then drag the fill handle down the column.
Step 7. Search Schema
Repeat on every site collection, using the same numbers everywhere. This is what makes values from different sites land in the same hub filter.
First, confirm the crawled properties exist. Site settings, Search Schema, Crawled Properties, search for CEDoc. If nothing comes back, no tagged file has been crawled yet. Tag a few files, wait 30 to 60 minutes, and check again. Crawled properties are shared across the whole tenant, so once they appear on one site they are available everywhere.
